  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:agent-runtime",
  "domain": "ai",
  "definition": "An Agent Runtime is the infrastructure execution layer that manages the complete lifecycle, resource allocation, tool access, memory state, and communication channels of one or more autonomous AI agents \u2014 providing process isolation, context window management, stateful execution with durable checkpointing, sandboxed tool-call dispatch, inter-agent messaging, credential management, rate limiting, and structured observability, analogous to how an operating system runtime supports application processes, and forming the foundational services upon which Agent Orchestrator control logic and Agentic Workflow execution patterns are built.",
